{"entries":[{"id":"scofield-es-2ki-1-3","title":"2 Reyes 1:3","author":"C. I. Scofield (1843–1921)","reference":{"book":"2KI","chapterStart":1,"verseStart":3,"chapterEnd":1,"verseEnd":3},"content":"<p>Introducción al libro - 2 Reyes Lea el primer capítulo de 2 Reyes. Este libro continúa la historia de los reinos hasta los cautiverios. Incluye la traducción de Elías y el ministerio de Eliseo. Durante este período profetizaron Amós y Oseas en Israel, y Abdías, Joel, Isaías, Miqueas, Nahúm, Habacuc, Sofonías y Jeremías en Judá. Segunda de Reyes consta de siete partes: El último ministerio y la traducción de Elías, 1:1-2:11. El ministerio de Eliseo desde el traslado de Elías hasta la unción de Jehú, 2:12-9:10. El reinado de Jehú sobre Israel, 9:11-10:36. Los reinados de Atalía y Joás sobre Judá, 11:1-12:21. Los reinados de Joacaz y Joás sobre Israel y el último ministerio de Eliseo, 13:1-25. Desde la muerte de Eliseo hasta el cautiverio de Israel, 14:1-17:41. Desde el ascenso de Ezequías al cautiverio de Judá, 18:1-25:30. Los acontecimientos registrados en Segunda de Reyes cubren un período de 308 años. (Ussher) ángel (véase Scofield &quot;Hebreos 1:4&quot;).</p>","translation":{"sourceId":"scofield-2ki-1-3","status":"official","sourceLanguage":"en","targetLanguage":"es"}},{"id":"scofield-es-2ki-1-15","title":"2 Reyes 1:15","author":"C. I. Scofield (1843–1921)","reference":{"book":"2KI","chapterStart":1,"verseStart":15,"chapterEnd":1,"verseEnd":15},"content":"<p>ángel (véase Scofield &quot;Hebreos 1:4&quot;).</p>","translation":{"sourceId":"scofield-2ki-1-15","status":"official","sourceLanguage":"en","targetLanguage":"es"}},{"id":"scofield-es-2ki-4-1","title":"2 Reyes 4:1","author":"C. I. Scofield (1843–1921)","reference":{"book":"2KI","chapterStart":4,"verseStart":1,"chapterEnd":4,"verseEnd":1},"content":"<p>miedo (véase Scofield &quot;Salmo 19:9&quot;).</p>","translation":{"sourceId":"scofield-2ki-4-1","status":"official","sourceLanguage":"en","targetLanguage":"es"}},{"id":"scofield-es-2ki-4-27","title":"2 Reyes 4:27","author":"C. I. Scofield (1843–1921)","reference":{"book":"2KI","chapterStart":4,"verseStart":27,"chapterEnd":4,"verseEnd":27},"content":"<p>heb. &quot;amargo.&quot; 1 Samuel 1:10.</p>","translation":{"sourceId":"scofield-2ki-4-27","status":"official","sourceLanguage":"en","targetLanguage":"es"}},{"id":"scofield-es-2ki-5-12","title":"2 Reyes 5:12","author":"C. I. Scofield (1843–1921)","reference":{"book":"2KI","chapterStart":5,"verseStart":12,"chapterEnd":5,"verseEnd":12},"content":"<p>Abana O, Amana.</p>","translation":{"sourceId":"scofield-2ki-5-12","status":"official","sourceLanguage":"en","targetLanguage":"es"}},{"id":"scofield-es-2ki-5-25","title":"2 Reyes 5:25","author":"C. I. Scofield (1843–1921)","reference":{"book":"2KI","chapterStart":5,"verseStart":25,"chapterEnd":5,"verseEnd":25},"content":"<p>en ninguna parte Heb. &quot;ni aquí ni allá.&quot;</p>","translation":{"sourceId":"scofield-2ki-5-25","status":"official","sourceLanguage":"en","targetLanguage":"es"}},{"id":"scofield-es-2ki-8-16","title":"2 Reyes 8:16","author":"C. I. Scofield (1843–1921)","reference":{"book":"2KI","chapterStart":8,"verseStart":16,"chapterEnd":8,"verseEnd":16},"content":"<p>Joram llamado Joram, 2 Reyes 8:21,23,24. comenzó heb. reinó, es decir, comenzó a reinar en consorte con su padre.</p>","translation":{"sourceId":"scofield-2ki-8-16","status":"official","sourceLanguage":"en","targetLanguage":"es"}},{"id":"scofield-es-2ki-10-15","title":"2 Reyes 10:15","author":"C. I. Scofield (1843–1921)","reference":{"book":"2KI","chapterStart":10,"verseStart":15,"chapterEnd":10,"verseEnd":15},"content":"<p>Jonadab llamado Jonadab, Jeremías 35:6,8,10,14,16,18,19.</p>","translation":{"sourceId":"scofield-2ki-10-15","status":"official","sourceLanguage":"en","targetLanguage":"es"}},{"id":"scofield-es-2ki-14-7","title":"2 Reyes 14:7","author":"C. I. Scofield (1843–1921)","reference":{"book":"2KI","chapterStart":14,"verseStart":7,"chapterEnd":14,"verseEnd":7},"content":"<p>Edom Ver 2 Crónicas 25:5-16.</p>","translation":{"sourceId":"scofield-2ki-14-7","status":"official","sourceLanguage":"en","targetLanguage":"es"}},{"id":"scofield-es-2ki-14-21","title":"2 Reyes 14:21","author":"C. I. Scofield (1843–1921)","reference":{"book":"2KI","chapterStart":14,"verseStart":21,"chapterEnd":14,"verseEnd":21},"content":"<p>Azarías llamado Uzías, 2 Crónicas 26:1; Isaías 1:1.</p>","translation":{"sourceId":"scofield-2ki-14-21","status":"official","sourceLanguage":"en","targetLanguage":"es"}},{"id":"scofield-es-2ki-14-29","title":"2 Reyes 14:29","author":"C. I. Scofield (1843–1921)","reference":{"book":"2KI","chapterStart":14,"verseStart":29,"chapterEnd":14,"verseEnd":29},"content":"<p>Zacarías Después de un interregno de 11 años. 2 Reyes 15:8.</p>","translation":{"sourceId":"scofield-2ki-14-29","status":"official","sourceLanguage":"en","targetLanguage":"es"}},{"id":"scofield-es-2ki-15-1","title":"2 Reyes 15:1","author":"C. I. Scofield (1843–1921)","reference":{"book":"2KI","chapterStart":15,"verseStart":1,"chapterEnd":15,"verseEnd":1},"content":"<p>Zacarías Después de un interregno de 11 años. 2 Reyes 15:8.</p>","translation":{"sourceId":"scofield-2ki-15-1","status":"official","sourceLanguage":"en","targetLanguage":"es"}},{"id":"scofield-es-2ki-15-10","title":"2 Reyes 15:10","author":"C. I. Scofield (1843–1921)","reference":{"book":"2KI","chapterStart":15,"verseStart":10,"chapterEnd":15,"verseEnd":10},"content":"<p>hirió como se profetizó, Amós 7:9.</p>","translation":{"sourceId":"scofield-2ki-15-10","status":"official","sourceLanguage":"en","targetLanguage":"es"}},{"id":"scofield-es-2ki-15-13","title":"2 Reyes 15:13","author":"C. I. Scofield (1843–1921)","reference":{"book":"2KI","chapterStart":15,"verseStart":13,"chapterEnd":15,"verseEnd":13},"content":"<p>Uzías Mateo 1:8,9 llamado Ozías 2 Reyes 15:7 llamado Azarías.</p>","translation":{"sourceId":"scofield-2ki-15-13","status":"official","sourceLanguage":"en","targetLanguage":"es"}},{"id":"scofield-es-2ki-17-7","title":"2 Reyes 17:7","author":"C. I. Scofield (1843–1921)","reference":{"book":"2KI","chapterStart":17,"verseStart":7,"chapterEnd":17,"verseEnd":7},"content":"<p>pecó cf. Deuteronomio 28:15-68. Desde este cautiverio las diez tribus nunca han sido restituidas a Palestina. Un remanente de Judá regresó bajo Zorobabel, Esdras y Nehemías, y individuos de las diez tribus (llamadas, después de la división del reino de Salomón, &quot;Israel&quot; en los libros históricos y Profetas, también &quot;Efraín&quot; por este último) regresaron, pero la restauración nacional aún no se ha cumplido. Ver Pacto Palestino, (véase Scofield &quot;Deuteronomio 30:3&quot;), Reino, 2 Samuel 7:8-17.</p>","translation":{"sourceId":"scofield-2ki-17-7","status":"official","sourceLanguage":"en","targetLanguage":"es"}},{"id":"scofield-es-2ki-17-33","title":"2 Reyes 17:33","author":"C. I. Scofield (1843–1921)","reference":{"book":"2KI","chapterStart":17,"verseStart":33,"chapterEnd":17,"verseEnd":33},"content":"<p>temido (véase Scofield &quot;Salmo 19:9&quot;).</p>","translation":{"sourceId":"scofield-2ki-17-33","status":"official","sourceLanguage":"en","targetLanguage":"es"}},{"id":"scofield-es-2ki-17-36","title":"2 Reyes 17:36","author":"C. I. Scofield (1843–1921)","reference":{"book":"2KI","chapterStart":17,"verseStart":36,"chapterEnd":17,"verseEnd":36},"content":"<p>miedo (véase Scofield &quot;Salmo 19:9&quot;).</p>","translation":{"sourceId":"scofield-2ki-17-36","status":"official","sourceLanguage":"en","targetLanguage":"es"}},{"id":"scofield-es-2ki-17-39","title":"2 Reyes 17:39","author":"C. I. Scofield (1843–1921)","reference":{"book":"2KI","chapterStart":17,"verseStart":39,"chapterEnd":17,"verseEnd":39},"content":"<p>miedo (véase Scofield &quot;Salmo 19:9&quot;).</p>","translation":{"sourceId":"scofield-2ki-17-39","status":"official","sourceLanguage":"en","targetLanguage":"es"}},{"id":"scofield-es-2ki-17-41","title":"2 Reyes 17:41","author":"C. I. Scofield (1843–1921)","reference":{"book":"2KI","chapterStart":17,"verseStart":41,"chapterEnd":17,"verseEnd":41},"content":"<p>temido (véase Scofield &quot;Salmo 19:9&quot;).</p>","translation":{"sourceId":"scofield-2ki-17-41","status":"official","sourceLanguage":"en","targetLanguage":"es"}},{"id":"scofield-es-2ki-18-1","title":"2 Reyes 18:1","author":"C. I. Scofield (1843–1921)","reference":{"book":"2KI","chapterStart":18,"verseStart":1,"chapterEnd":18,"verseEnd":1},"content":"<p>temido (véase Scofield &quot;Salmo 19:9&quot;).</p>","translation":{"sourceId":"scofield-2ki-18-1","status":"official","sourceLanguage":"en","targetLanguage":"es"}},{"id":"scofield-es-2ki-18-4","title":"2 Reyes 18:4","author":"C. I. Scofield (1843–1921)","reference":{"book":"2KI","chapterStart":18,"verseStart":4,"chapterEnd":18,"verseEnd":4},"content":"<p>bosques sagrados (véase Scofield &quot;Deuteronomio 16:21&quot;).</p>","translation":{"sourceId":"scofield-2ki-18-4","status":"official","sourceLanguage":"en","targetLanguage":"es"}},{"id":"scofield-es-2ki-18-5","title":"2 Reyes 18:5","author":"C. I. Scofield (1843–1921)","reference":{"book":"2KI","chapterStart":18,"verseStart":5,"chapterEnd":18,"verseEnd":5},"content":"<p>confiable (véase Scofield &quot;Salmo 2:12&quot;).</p>","translation":{"sourceId":"scofield-2ki-18-5","status":"official","sourceLanguage":"en","targetLanguage":"es"}},{"id":"scofield-es-2ki-18-11","title":"2 Reyes 18:11","author":"C. I. Scofield (1843–1921)","reference":{"book":"2KI","chapterStart":18,"verseStart":11,"chapterEnd":18,"verseEnd":11},"content":"<p>sí llevó Tiempos de los Gentiles. 2 Reyes 18:9,12; 2 Reyes 25:1-21; Lucas 21:24; Apocalipsis 16:19.</p>","translation":{"sourceId":"scofield-2ki-18-11","status":"official","sourceLanguage":"en","targetLanguage":"es"}},{"id":"scofield-es-2ki-19-2","title":"2 Reyes 19:2","author":"C. I. Scofield (1843–1921)","reference":{"book":"2KI","chapterStart":19,"verseStart":2,"chapterEnd":19,"verseEnd":2},"content":"<p>Isaías llamado Isaías, Lucas 3:4.</p>","translation":{"sourceId":"scofield-2ki-19-2","status":"official","sourceLanguage":"en","targetLanguage":"es"}},{"id":"scofield-es-2ki-19-10","title":"2 Reyes 19:10","author":"C. I. Scofield (1843–1921)","reference":{"book":"2KI","chapterStart":19,"verseStart":10,"chapterEnd":19,"verseEnd":10},"content":"<p>más confiable (véase Scofield &quot;Salmo 2:12&quot;).</p>","translation":{"sourceId":"scofield-2ki-19-10","status":"official","sourceLanguage":"en","targetLanguage":"es"}},{"id":"scofield-es-2ki-19-35","title":"2 Reyes 19:35","author":"C. I. Scofield (1843–1921)","reference":{"book":"2KI","chapterStart":19,"verseStart":35,"chapterEnd":19,"verseEnd":35},"content":"<p>ángel (véase Scofield &quot;Hebreos 1:4&quot;).</p>","translation":{"sourceId":"scofield-2ki-19-35","status":"official","sourceLanguage":"en","targetLanguage":"es"}},{"id":"scofield-es-2ki-20-18","title":"2 Reyes 20:18","author":"C. I. Scofield (1843–1921)","reference":{"book":"2KI","chapterStart":20,"verseStart":18,"chapterEnd":20,"verseEnd":18},"content":"<p>Se cumplirán. Daniel 1:3.</p>","translation":{"sourceId":"scofield-2ki-20-18","status":"official","sourceLanguage":"en","targetLanguage":"es"}},{"id":"scofield-es-2ki-21-26","title":"2 Reyes 21:26","author":"C. I. Scofield (1843–1921)","reference":{"book":"2KI","chapterStart":21,"verseStart":26,"chapterEnd":21,"verseEnd":26},"content":"<p>Josías llamó a Josías, Mateo 1:10.</p>","translation":{"sourceId":"scofield-2ki-21-26","status":"official","sourceLanguage":"en","targetLanguage":"es"}},{"id":"scofield-es-2ki-22-1","title":"2 Reyes 22:1","author":"C. I. Scofield (1843–1921)","reference":{"book":"2KI","chapterStart":22,"verseStart":1,"chapterEnd":22,"verseEnd":1},"content":"<p>Josías llamó a Josías, Mateo 1:10.</p>","translation":{"sourceId":"scofield-2ki-22-1","status":"official","sourceLanguage":"en","targetLanguage":"es"}},{"id":"scofield-es-2ki-23-6","title":"2 Reyes 23:6","author":"C. I. Scofield (1843–1921)","reference":{"book":"2KI","chapterStart":23,"verseStart":6,"chapterEnd":23,"verseEnd":6},"content":"<p>bosque sagrado (véase Scofield &quot;Deuteronomio 16:21&quot;).</p>","translation":{"sourceId":"scofield-2ki-23-6","status":"official","sourceLanguage":"en","targetLanguage":"es"}},{"id":"scofield-es-2ki-23-13","title":"2 Reyes 23:13","author":"C. I. Scofield (1843–1921)","reference":{"book":"2KI","chapterStart":23,"verseStart":13,"chapterEnd":23,"verseEnd":13},"content":"<p>Astoret 2 Reyes 23:6,7. (véase Scofield &quot;Jueces 2:13&quot;).</p>","translation":{"sourceId":"scofield-2ki-23-13","status":"official","sourceLanguage":"en","targetLanguage":"es"}},{"id":"scofield-es-2ki-23-34","title":"2 Reyes 23:34","author":"C. I. Scofield (1843–1921)","reference":{"book":"2KI","chapterStart":23,"verseStart":34,"chapterEnd":23,"verseEnd":34},"content":"<p>Joacim llamado Jakim. Mateo 1:10,11. (véase Scofield &quot;Mateo 1:10&quot;).</p>","translation":{"sourceId":"scofield-2ki-23-34","status":"official","sourceLanguage":"en","targetLanguage":"es"}},{"id":"scofield-es-2ki-24-8","title":"2 Reyes 24:8","author":"C. I. Scofield (1843–1921)","reference":{"book":"2KI","chapterStart":24,"verseStart":8,"chapterEnd":24,"verseEnd":8},"content":"<p>dieciocho cf. 2 Crónicas 36:9; 1 Corintios 10:8. (véase Scofield &quot;1 Corintios 10:8&quot;).</p>","translation":{"sourceId":"scofield-2ki-24-8","status":"official","sourceLanguage":"en","targetLanguage":"es"}},{"id":"scofield-es-2ki-24-12","title":"2 Reyes 24:12","author":"C. I. Scofield (1843–1921)","reference":{"book":"2KI","chapterStart":24,"verseStart":12,"chapterEnd":24,"verseEnd":12},"content":"<p>El octavo año del rey Nabucodonosor. Jeremías 25:1.</p>","translation":{"sourceId":"scofield-2ki-24-12","status":"official","sourceLanguage":"en","targetLanguage":"es"}},{"id":"scofield-es-2ki-25-1","title":"2 Reyes 25:1","author":"C. I. Scofield (1843–1921)","reference":{"book":"2KI","chapterStart":25,"verseStart":1,"chapterEnd":25,"verseEnd":1},"content":"<p>décimo, es decir, enero.</p>","translation":{"sourceId":"scofield-2ki-25-1","status":"official","sourceLanguage":"en","targetLanguage":"es"}},{"id":"scofield-es-2ki-25-3","title":"2 Reyes 25:3","author":"C. I. Scofield (1843–1921)","reference":{"book":"2KI","chapterStart":25,"verseStart":3,"chapterEnd":25,"verseEnd":3},"content":"<p>cuarto mes, es decir, julio.</p>","translation":{"sourceId":"scofield-2ki-25-3","status":"official","sourceLanguage":"en","targetLanguage":"es"}},{"id":"scofield-es-2ki-25-4","title":"2 Reyes 25:4","author":"C. I. Scofield (1843–1921)","reference":{"book":"2KI","chapterStart":25,"verseStart":4,"chapterEnd":25,"verseEnd":4},"content":"<p>Y la ciudad Tiempos de los gentiles. 2 Reyes 25:1-21; Daniel 2:29-45; Lucas 21:24; Apocalipsis 16:19.</p>","translation":{"sourceId":"scofield-2ki-25-4","status":"official","sourceLanguage":"en","targetLanguage":"es"}},{"id":"scofield-es-2ki-25-8","title":"2 Reyes 25:8","author":"C. I. Scofield (1843–1921)","reference":{"book":"2KI","chapterStart":25,"verseStart":8,"chapterEnd":25,"verseEnd":8},"content":"<p>quinto, es decir, agosto.</p>","translation":{"sourceId":"scofield-2ki-25-8","status":"official","sourceLanguage":"en","targetLanguage":"es"}},{"id":"scofield-es-2ki-25-25","title":"2 Reyes 25:25","author":"C. I. Scofield (1843–1921)","reference":{"book":"2KI","chapterStart":25,"verseStart":25,"chapterEnd":25,"verseEnd":25},"content":"<p>séptimo mes, es decir, octubre.</p>","translation":{"sourceId":"scofield-2ki-25-25","status":"official","sourceLanguage":"en","targetLanguage":"es"}},{"id":"scofield-es-2ki-25-27","title":"2 Reyes 25:27","author":"C. I. Scofield (1843–1921)","reference":{"book":"2KI","chapterStart":25,"verseStart":27,"chapterEnd":25,"verseEnd":27},"content":"<p>duodécimo mes, es decir, marzo.</p>","translation":{"sourceId":"scofield-2ki-25-27","status":"official","sourceLanguage":"en","targetLanguage":"es"}}]}
